\section*{Joint metric, spectrum and heat-trace limit for FK–Ising maps}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. For critical FK--Ising spherical maps, the authors claim joint convergence of ordered eigenvalues and positive-time heat traces to the Liouville Brownian spectrum, with time multiplied by the number of edges.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
The argument takes coupled conformal and metric limits as inputs and proves conductivity one for the unnormalized graph energy. Local recovery and convergence of centered inverse operators identify the limiting Dirichlet form and its compact resolvent, which then yield eigenvalue and heat-trace convergence.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
For critical FK--Ising spherical maps, the authors claim joint convergence of ordered eigenvalues and positive-time heat traces to the Liouville Brownian spectrum, with time multiplied by the number of edges. The question retains these same parameters and conventions. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 211, the selected Lean theorem is the $q>4$ Brownian tree metric-measure limit, with degree measure and the $n^{-1/2}$ distance scale. The subcritical, critical-Liouville, walk, and spectral companions are not included. No Comparator is assigned to the selected manuscript here; the family page selects other papers or supporting statements. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

